Venetium 0053 - fixes from the full review of patches 0001-0051 (C:\handoff\PATCH-REVIEW.md, 2026-10-15, his "fix all").
Each item names the patch it corrects; the review's ids are in brackets.
- 0047 [B1, B2] dxva_video_decoder.cc: the D3D11 decode bridge could never run - ProbeMaxDecodeSize only looked at
  ANGLE's D3D9 device, which a D3D11 render path does not have, so the probe always failed first - and its output had no
  ordering between our D3D9 device and ANGLE's D3D11 device. The probe and the decoder now share GetDecodeD3D9DeviceEx()
  (ANGLE's D3D9Ex device; else, on the D3D11 path, one standalone D3D9Ex device per GPU process), and after the
  NV12 -> RGB StretchRect on that own device an event query is flushed and polled (at most 250 ms) before the D3D11 side
  samples the shared texture. The bridge has never run on hardware and the Adreno it is for has the bad D3D9 driver, so it
  is behind the feature VenetiumDxvaD3D11Bridge, DISABLED by default (--enable-features=VenetiumDxvaD3D11Bridge to try
  it). The Tegra path (ANGLE on D3D9, ANGLE's own device) is unchanged.
- 0041 [P1] dxva_video_decoder.cc: kNumPictureBuffers 8 -> 6, the renderer's queue (limits::kMaxVideoFrames = 4) plus the
  frame being composited and the one on screen; ~16 MB less of the Tegra's shared memory at 1080p (Chromium 77 used 5).
- 0020 [B3] capture_context_win_arm.asm: CaptureContext stored LR (Thumb bit set) as Pc, a CPSR without the T bit and no
  VFP state. Now Pc = LR & ~1, Cpsr = APSR | T, D0-D31 and Fpscr are stored and ContextFlags is CONTEXT_ARM | CONTROL |
  INTEGER | FLOATING_POINT (0x200007); r1/r2 are restored before returning. Crash-report quality only (dumps taken from a
  captured context now unwind from the right instruction and carry the VFP registers).
- 0049 [B4] software_rendering_list.json: the ANGLE-D3D9 GPU-raster exception matched any Direct3D9 renderer, so on x86
  chrome://flags#use-angle=d3d9 turned GPU raster on for old D3D9 GPUs too. It is now scoped by the DXGI vendor ids the
  ARM32 SoCs report - NVIDIA 0x4144564e ('NVDA': Tegra 3 and 4) and, as its own exception, Qualcomm 0x4d4f4351 ('QCOM':
  Adreno on D3D9) - which x86 GPUs (PCI ids 0x10de/0x8086/0x1002) never report. 0051's Adreno D3D11 entry is unchanged.
- 0029 [S1] sandbox_policy_base.cc + process_mitigations.cc: on ARM32 the creation-time mitigation attribute is dropped
  (build 15035 refuses it), so the extension-point, non-system-font and image-load (no remote / no low label) policies
  were never applied - while the child was told they were. On ARM32 the broker now re-homes those four into the delayed
  set (the conversion AddAppContainerProfile() already does for its CreateProcess bug) and transfers an empty startup
  set, and the child applies them after startup, best-effort: a refusal leaves that flag off instead of hitting
  SetProcessMitigationPolicyInternal's PCHECK. Other platforms keep the fatal path, byte-for-byte the same behaviour.
- 0019 [S2] service_resolver_arm.cc: FlushInstructionCache on the child after writing the interception thunks (the copied
  original and the patched ntdll stub); ARMv7's instruction cache is not coherent with data writes, and nothing documents
  that WriteProcessMemory flushes. resolver_arm.cc: comment only (the in-place EAT thunk is not flushed; on ARM32 its only
  user is the CreateThread interception, armed only for CSRSS-disconnected children, none since 0030).
- 0032 [P3] ProgramExecutableD3D.{h,cpp}: the failed-compile cache was keyed by the full generated HLSL, so every draw on
  a too-large Skia program still regenerated its vertex/pixel HLSL just to look it up. It is now keyed by the executable's
  signature (vertex input signature or pixel output layout, plus the image2D bind layout) - at least as specific as
  ANGLE's own executable cache - and checked before any HLSL is generated; reset() clears it with the rest of the link.
  The serialized program format is unchanged.
- 0045 [P4] gl_features.cc: the one-shot D3D11 probe passes ppDevice = ppImmediateContext = nullptr, so
  D3D11CreateDevice only reports the feature level (S_FALSE) instead of creating a device and context to throw away.
- 0025 [P5] cpuinfo arm/windows/init.c: report idiv, fma and fp16 when Windows reports hardware divide
  (PF_ARM_DIVIDE_INSTRUCTION_AVAILABLE) - every ARMv7 core with it (Cortex-A15, Krait: Tegra 4, the Lumias) is ARMv7VE with
  VFPv4. Cortex-A9 (Tegra 3) reports none and stays on the baseline, so XNNPACK/ruy pick their NEON-FMA kernels only where
  VFMA exists.
- 0012 supermium_flag_entries.h: flag text typos - "mimick" -> "mimic", "Windows 11 Mica Taskbar" -> "Titlebar" (the flag is
  windows11-mica-titlebar), "Diasble" -> "Disable". Internal flag names are unchanged (renaming would reset users' flags).
- 0043 (description only): it said the USER_LIMITED renderer keeps "win32k lockdown, all mitigations"; on ARM32 0030 dropped
  the win32k lockdown and 0029 the creation-time mitigations. 0043's header text is corrected in place; its diff is untouched.
NOT changed (see the review): P2, the MFT running on the GPU main thread, needs a device trace first; P6, BoringSSL without
asm on ARM32, is not worth it (ChaCha20 in C outruns the Wi-Fi); P7, prediction/preconnect off, is a privacy choice.
Device: none of these are device-tested yet. Structural gates pass on both arches (ARMNT/I386, CFG, no new DLL imports,
identical exports, the 15035 kernel32/ntdll import check, CaptureContext's VFP stores linked into all three crashpad users).

